<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="AARCH64:LE:64:v8A:default">
<!--
    Mach-O Core Foundation constant strings (`option cfstrings on|off`).

    Issue: a `CFSTR("x")` compiles to a four-word CFString struct in
    `__cfstring` (isa, flags, char pointer, length). Code references the
    struct, not the characters, so the constant-string route, which reads
    the bytes AT the referenced address, sees the struct and prints the
    entry address. On the Toyota iOS app (84 MB arm64) kuna printed
    `NSLog(0x1044376b0)` for `NSLog(CFSTR("Reachability Flag Status: ..."))`.

    Stage / sub-stage: P1 external-refinement, the Mach-O `cfstrings`
    analysis pass (`kuna-analysis/src/analyzers/cfstring/mod.rs`), whose
    facts the commit seam turns into a `char[N]` entry plus a StringManager
    seed at the entry address (`kuna-console/src/engine.rs`).

    P0 assertion: `option cfstrings on|off` (default off). It is a commit-time
    gate, so it is set after `load file` and before the `read symbols` that
    commits the analysis.

    The XML wrapper only supplies the harness architecture. Both passes clear
    it and load the real arm64 Mach-O fixture `macho_cfstring` (built from
    `macho_cfstring.c`, see the fixtures README): one hand-built CFString
    constant `{ ___CFConstantStringClassReference, 0x7c8, "cfstring hello",
    14 }` in `__DATA_CONST,__cfstring` @0x100004008 and `_get_greeting`
    @0x100000538 returning its address.

    Pass 1 (the default, the BUG): `_get_greeting` returns the bare entry
    address `0x100004008`. Pass 2 (`option cfstrings on`, the FIX): it returns
    the literal `"cfstring hello"`.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
c0035fd6
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/macho_cfstring</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>load addr 0x100000538</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/macho_cfstring</com>
  <com>option cfstrings on</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>load addr 0x100000538</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="cfstrings off: the __cfstring reference is the bare entry address" min="1" max="1">return 0x100004008;</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="cfstrings on: the __cfstring reference renders its string literal" min="1" max="1">return "cfstring hello";</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="cfstrings on: the returned constant is typed as a char pointer" min="1" max="1">char \* _get_greeting\(void\)</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
